  "body": "The `site` job of `release.yml` run 44976953856 (tag v0.25.0, commit 7e2a8119c) failed at the step \"Site tests\" (`python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v`). So the `pages` job does not deploy \"CamCraft 0.25.0\".\n\nThis step is new in this release (PR #2643). Nothing else runs these tests, so they drifted since v0.24.0. A local run with the pinned zola 0.23.6 shows 73 failures and 1 error on v0.25.0. `main` at dfbe0d8a5 fails the same way (74 failures, 1 error). The failures come from the tree, not from the runner.\n\nCauses:\n\n1. 44 icon-position failures (`site/tests/test_guide_icons.py:118`, and `test_guide_refresh.py:50`). Each operation section now starts with the `catalog:examples` block, and the icon comes after it. Cause: b8e217cb8.\n2. Missing site icons: `site/static/icons/{op-slot-undercut,tool-t-slot,tool-keyseat,tool-dovetail,tool-lollipop}.png` (`test_guide_icons.py:165`). The app icons exist in `assets/ui/`. Cause: 5452810e5 (#2714).\n3. Slot Undercut has no section in the operation reference (`test_operation_reference.py:58`). Cause: 5452810e5.\n4. The post manifest property `rotariesBeforeTraverse` has no row in the site post-processor reference (`test_post_processor_reference.py:23`). Cause: 56e81ffc8.\n5. The MCP guide lost the fact \"no live transport endpoint\" (`test_guide_after_1995.py:18`). Cause: 028495f5c.\n6. `test_first_continuous_4axis_part` reads `docs/decisions/1904-continuous-4axis-walkthrough.md`, but the cut moves each decision file into `RECOMMENDED.md`. The test must not read a file under `docs/decisions/`.\n7. 18 UI label failures (`test_first_4axis_part.py:173` and the continuous twin). The tool Properties no longer draw the labels as plain string literals. Causes: 97f6cb595, 963d7c381.\n\nExpected: the site tests pass on `main`. The fix changes the guide content, the site icons and the tests so that they match the shipped app. It does not weaken a check without a reason in the PR.\n\nThe tag v0.25.0 does not move. After the fix, the coordinator decides how the 0.25.0 site is published, and records the decision on this issue.\n",
